{#
   Contextual admin actions, rendered next to the thing they act on.

   Most edits concern something the person is already looking at, so an admin
   reading an event should not have to go and find that event again in the panel.
   Global configuration stays in the panel; this is only for "this record, here".

   ⚠️ **This is a shortcut, never a permission.** Everything it links to lives
   behind `/admin` or `/staff`, which `security.yaml` gates with `access_control`
   — so the button appearing is a convenience and the button *working* is decided
   server-side, by the firewall, on every request. Hiding it from an anonymous
   visitor is presentation; it is not what stops them.

   ⚠️ **You no longer name the role — the route's own rule decides (S49).** Each
   action is shown when `can_reach()` says the firewall would let this person open
   it, which asks the very `access_control` map the firewall itself consults. That
   removes a whole class of bug, because **this app has no role hierarchy**:
   `ROLE_ADMIN` does not imply `ROLE_STAFF`, so hand-writing `ROLE_STAFF` on a chip
   whose route sits under `/admin` hid it from the only people who could use it
   (the event-registrations chip, S30), and the opposite offers a button that
   bounces to `/login`. An explicit `role:` is still honoured for the rare case
   where an action needs to be *stricter* than its route.

   Nothing is emitted at all for a visitor without the role, so a public page's
   markup is unchanged for the people who actually read it.

   Usage:
     {% from 'site/_admin_inline.html.twig' import admin_actions %}
     {{ admin_actions([
         { route: 'app_admin_event_edit', params: { id: event.id }, label: 'edit'|trans },
         { route: 'app_admin_event_registrations', params: { id: event.id }, label: '…' },
     ]) }}
#}
{% macro admin_actions(actions, role) %}
    {# `role` (on the macro or on an action) is now an optional *extra* restriction
       on top of the route's own rule, not a replacement for it. #}
    {% set visible = actions|filter(a =>
        can_reach(a.route, a.params|default({}))
        and (a.role|default(role) is null or is_granted(a.role|default(role)))
    ) %}
    {% if visible is not empty %}
        <span class="admin-inline" role="group" aria-label="{{ 'admin_inline.label'|trans }}">
            {% for a in visible %}
                <a class="admin-inline__action" href="{{ path(a.route, a.params|default({})) }}">
                    <svg class="admin-inline__icon" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                        <path d="M13.6 2.4a1.4 1.4 0 0 1 2 2l-8.5 8.5-2.7.7.7-2.7 8.5-8.5Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                        <path d="M3 17h14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                    </svg>
                    {{ a.label }}
                </a>
            {% endfor %}
        </span>
    {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
